WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.960
Here's a strip of paint colours,
sliding smoothly from green to blue.

2
00:00:05.010 --> 00:00:07.350
In English, we split it in two.

3
00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:08.580
Green at one end.

4
00:00:08.630 --> 00:00:09.940
Blue at the other.

5
00:00:09.990 --> 00:00:14.110
But what if your language had
just one word for the whole strip?

6
00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:17.970
Would you actually see those colours
differently from an English speaker?

7
00:00:18.020 --> 00:00:21.130
In this mission, you'll
tackle a big question.

8
00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:25.700
Does language depend on thought, or
does thinking depend on language?

9
00:00:25.750 --> 00:00:29.200
You'll weigh up whether a missing
word limits what you can think,

10
00:00:29.250 --> 00:00:31.540
or just nudges what you notice.

11
00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:35.640
And you'll test the idea against
colour words from different languages.

12
00:00:35.690 --> 00:00:40.620
Your mission: decide whether people with
one word for green and blue see colour

13
00:00:40.670 --> 00:00:41.560
differently.
